Relevant columns and why they matter  
• `event_date`:   limits the query to the 2020‑12 tables (`20201201` … `20201231`).  
• `event_name`:   equals `'page_view'` for every page‑view hit we want to count.  
• `event_params`: repeated record that stores the parameters we need:  
  • `key = 'page_location'` → `value.string_value` holds the full URL.  
  • (optionally) `key = 'page_path'` can be inspected but is often empty in GA4 export.  
• Conditions that will be used  
  event_date BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'  
  event_name = 'page_view'  
  LOWER(page_host) = 'shop.googlemerchandisestore.com'  

Below are ten exploratory → analytical SQL statements (all with LIMIT 20) that progressively lead to the answer “Which page has the 2nd‑highest total page‑views on that host in Dec‑2020 after cleaning the path?”.  
All queries reference the BigQuery public GA4 export:

project.dataset = `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce`

```sql
--1. Description: List the different event names that exist in December 2020 (sanity‑check).
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2. Description: Grab 20 raw rows of the page_view event to inspect parameters.
SELECT event_date,
       event_timestamp,
       event_params
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3. Description: Pull the page_location parameter for a handful of rows.
SELECT event_date,
       (SELECT value.string_value
        FROM UNNEST(event_params)
        WHERE key = 'page_location')            AS page_location
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4. Description: Show the distribution of hosts for page_view events in December 2020.
SELECT SPLIT(page_location,'/')[OFFSET(2)]       AS page_host,
       COUNT(*)                                  AS pv
FROM (
  SELECT (SELECT value.string_value
          FROM UNNEST(event_params)
          WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
  WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
)
GROUP BY page_host
ORDER BY pv DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5. Description: Fetch 20 sample URLs only for the target host.
SELECT page_location
FROM (
  SELECT (SELECT value.string_value
          FROM UNNEST(event_params)
          WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
  WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
)
WHERE LOWER(SPLIT(page_location,'/')[OFFSET(2)]) = 'shop.googlemerchandisestore.com'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6. Description: Extract *raw* path (everything after the domain) and count.
SELECT SUBSTR(page_location, STRPOS(page_location, '/', 9)) AS raw_path,   -- 9 ≈ len('https://')
       COUNT(*)                                             AS pageviews
FROM (
  SELECT (SELECT value.string_value
          FROM UNNEST(event_params)
          WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
  WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
)
WHERE LOWER(SPLIT(page_location,'/')[OFFSET(2)]) = 'shop.googlemerchandisestore.com'
GROUP BY raw_path
ORDER BY pageviews DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7. Description: Clean up the path (collapse multiple slashes, drop query string & fragments).
SELECT REGEXP_REPLACE(
         REGEXP_EXTRACT(page_location, r'^[^?&#]+'),  -- keep URL before ? # &
         r'/{2,}', '/')                                -- collapse //, /// …
       AS clean_path,
       COUNT(*) AS pageviews
FROM (
  SELECT (SELECT value.string_value
          FROM UNNEST(event_params)
          WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
  WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
)
WHERE LOWER(SPLIT(page_location,'/')[OFFSET(2)]) = 'shop.googlemerchandisestore.com'
GROUP BY clean_path
ORDER BY pageviews DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8. Description: Same as #7 but rank the paths.
WITH paths AS (
  SELECT REGEXP_REPLACE(
           REGEXP_EXTRACT(page_location, r'^[^?&#]+'),
           r'/{2,}', '/')            AS clean_path,
         COUNT(*)                    AS pv
  FROM (
    SELECT (SELECT value.string_value
            FROM UNNEST(event_params)
            WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
    WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
  )
  WHERE LOWER(SPLIT(page_location,'/')[OFFSET(2)]) = 'shop.googlemerchandisestore.com'
  GROUP BY clean_path
)
SELECT clean_path,
       pv,
       DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY pv DESC) AS rnk
FROM paths
ORDER BY rnk, pv DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9. Description: Retrieve only the 2nd‑highest page (answer row).
WITH paths AS (
  SELECT REGEXP_REPLACE(
           REGEXP_EXTRACT(page_location, r'^[^?&#]+'),
           r'/{2,}', '/')            AS clean_path,
         COUNT(*)                    AS pv
  FROM (
    SELECT (SELECT value.string_value
            FROM UNNEST(event_params)
            WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
    WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
  )
  WHERE LOWER(SPLIT(page_location,'/')[OFFSET(2)]) = 'shop.googlemerchandisestore.com'
  GROUP BY clean_path
)
SELECT clean_path AS second_most_viewed_page,
       pv AS total_pageviews
FROM (
  SELECT clean_path,
         pv,
         DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY pv DESC) AS rnk
  FROM paths
)
WHERE rnk = 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Produce a full ordered list with rank, to cross‑check #9.
SELECT *
FROM (
  SELECT REGEXP_REPLACE(
           REGEXP_EXTRACT(page_location, r'^[^?&#]+'),
           r'/{2,}', '/')            AS clean_path,
         COUNT(*)                    AS pv,
         DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) AS rnk
  FROM (
    SELECT (SELECT value.string_value
            FROM UNNEST(event_params)
            WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202012*`
    WHERE event_name = 'page_view'
  )
  WHERE LOWER(SPLIT(page_location,'/')[OFFSET(2)]) = 'shop.googlemerchandisestore.com'
  GROUP BY clean_path
)
ORDER BY rnk, pv DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Running query #9 returns the single row that answers:  
